per-species occupancy recovery

  One row per species from a single fit of the 'base' scenario: 100 sites, 10
  species, 2 chains of 500 iterations after 500 burn-in. A row is flagged
  when it falls below a threshold one of the checks below uses.

  occ_true  Fraction of the 100 sites where the species really is present.
  occ_est   Fraction of sites where the model thinks it is present.
  psi_cor   How closely the estimated chance of being present tracks the true
            chance, across sites. Runs from -1 to 1; 0 means the estimates
            say nothing about where the species is.
  auc       Chance that the model rates a site where the species really is
            present above one where it really is absent. A coin flip scores
            0.5.
  drv_cov   This species has 3 coefficients setting where it is likely to be
            found: a baseline and 2 environmental effects. The model gives a
            plausible range for each. This is the share of those 3 ranges
            that contain the true value; it should be near 0.95.
  drv_err   Average distance between the model's best guess and the true
            value, over those same 3 coefficients. Smaller is better; it is
            on the scale of the coefficients themselves, so there is no fixed
            good value.

